@startuml
title Deadlock Playground - Deadlock Recovery Sequence

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequenceParticipant underline
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #777777
  ParticipantBorderColor #444444
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
  ActorBorderColor #444444
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #777777
  GroupBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
}

hide footbox
autonumber

actor User
participant "Browser\nAPI Client" as Client
participant "ApiServer" as API
participant "SessionStore" as Store
participant "SimulationEngine" as Engine
participant "DetectionStrategy" as Detector
participant "VictimPolicy" as Policy
participant "RecoveryStrategy" as Strategy
participant "Process / Resource\nDomain State" as Domain
participant "History" as History

User -> Client : Select policy and recovery strategy
User -> Client : Click Recover

Client -> API : POST /api/recover\n{policy, strategy}

API -> Store : Resolve browser session
Store --> API : Session-specific engine

API -> Engine : Execute recovery command

note over Engine
  Recovery operates only on the
  current browser session.

  The selected victim policy and
  recovery strategy are independent
  of prevention settings.
end note

Engine -> Detector : Detect current deadlock
Detector --> Engine : Detection result

alt No deadlock exists

  Engine --> API : NO_DEADLOCK error
  note over Engine,History
    No recovery transition is committed.
    Existing state and history remain intact.
  end note

else Deadlock detected

  loop While deadlock remains and an eligible intervention exists

    Engine -> Engine : Identify contended resource holders\non blocking deadlock relationships

    Engine -> Policy : Select victim from eligible processes
    Policy --> Engine : Selected victim

    Engine -> History : Stage VICTIM_SELECTED\nwith pre-intervention snapshot

    alt Strategy = TERMINATE

      Engine -> Strategy : Apply termination to victim

      Strategy -> Domain : Set victim state to TERMINATED
      Strategy -> Domain : Release all victim holdings
      Domain --> Strategy : Updated allocations

      Strategy --> Engine : Termination result

      Engine -> History : Stage TERMINATE event

    else Strategy = PREEMPT

      Engine -> Strategy : Apply preemption to victim

      Strategy -> Domain : Select contended exclusive resource
      Strategy -> Domain : Release victim holdings
      Strategy -> Domain : Roll back script execution\nand reset instruction progress
      Domain --> Strategy : Victim restored to RUNNING

      Strategy --> Engine : Preemption result

      Engine -> History : Stage PREEMPT and ROLLBACK events

    end

    Engine -> Domain : Reconsider pending resource requests
    Domain -> Domain : Grant eligible requests\nand update process states
    Domain --> Engine : Updated simulation state

    Engine -> Detector : Detect deadlock again
    Detector --> Engine : Updated detection result

    Engine -> History : Stage recovery-round events\nwith coherent resulting snapshots

  end

  alt Deadlock resolved

    Engine -> History : Stage RESOLVED event
    Engine -> History : Commit recovery history

    Engine --> API : Recovery result\nresolved = true

  else Deadlock remains after one or more rounds

    Engine -> History : Commit completed recovery rounds

    Engine --> API : Recovery result\nresolved = false

  else No eligible intervention was possible

    note over Engine,History
      No recovery round was committed.
      Preserve original state and history.
    end note

    Engine --> API : Recovery result\nrounds = [], resolved = false

  end

end

API --> Client : JSON response with result\nand current session state

Client -> Client : Refresh graph, processes,\nresources and event history

Client --> User : Display recovery outcome

note over Engine,History
  Victim-selection events represent the
  state before the intervention.

  Events completing a recovery round
  represent the state after resource
  release, wake-ups and redetection.

  An exception must not leave
  partially committed history.
end note

@enduml
